WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.962
Security tools process enormous amounts of data and generate valuable alerts, but no detection system has complete coverage.

2
00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:16.922
Rules reflect known conditions, available telemetry, configuration choices, thresholds, and assumptions about how threats will appear.

3
00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:27.708
Some activity may remain below an alert threshold, resemble legitimate work, occur in a poorly monitored environment, or use a pattern that existing analytics do not recognize.

4
00:00:27.708 --> 00:00:31.539
A missing alert therefore does not always mean an absence of risk.

5
00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:35.471
Threat hunting helps organizations investigate those uncertain areas.

6
00:00:35.471 --> 00:00:46.376
Analysts can ask whether an important scenario would be visible, whether expected evidence exists, and whether activity in the environment is consistent with normal business operations.

7
00:00:46.376 --> 00:00:51.136
This proactive work can reduce risk by finding suspicious activity earlier.

8
00:00:51.136 --> 00:01:02.979
Earlier understanding gives security teams more time to validate evidence, protect affected services, coordinate stakeholders, and decide whether incident-response procedures are necessary.

9
00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:05.803
Hunting also evaluates defensive assumptions.

10
00:01:05.803 --> 00:01:11.071
A team may believe that a data source is complete or that a detection covers a particular behavior.

11
00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:18.954
A hunt can reveal missing systems, inconsistent logging, noisy analytics, or conditions that the detection never considered.

12
00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:24.611
Organizations can use hunts to focus attention on high-value assets and business processes.

13
00:01:24.611 --> 00:01:36.834
Identity services, critical applications, sensitive data environments, and externally accessible services often deserve deeper visibility because their compromise could create greater impact.

14
00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:41.074
The value of hunting is broader than the number of confirmed threats found.

15
00:01:41.074 --> 00:01:50.304
Improvements to telemetry, asset ownership, analytical methods, detections, and cross-team communication all strengthen the security program.

16
00:01:50.304 --> 00:01:55.901
Threat hunting does not eliminate cyber risk, replace monitoring, or guarantee discovery.

17
00:01:55.901 --> 00:02:04.981
It adds a disciplined investigative capability that helps the organization learn about its environment and respond to gaps before they become larger problems.
